1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,362
Williams Obstetrics.

2
00:00:02,312 --> 00:00:06,587
Chapter 26: Induction and Augmentation of Labor.

3
00:00:06,587 --> 00:00:25,050
Labor Induction Preinduction Cervical Ripening Pharmacological Agents Mechanical Techniques Methods Of Induction And Augmentation Prostaglandin E1 Oxytocin Amniotomy For Induction And Augmentation References Today, several pharmacological agents permit labor to be induced or augmented.

4
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:33,050
Induction implies stimulation of contractions before the spontaneous onset of labor, with or without ruptured membranes.

5
00:00:33,050 --> 00:00:41,925
When the cervix is closed and uneffaced, labor induction is often preceded by cervical ripening, a process to soften and open the cervix.

6
00:00:41,925 --> 00:00:48,737
This is somewhat of a misnomer in that cervical ripening, per se, may also be a means of labor induction.

7
00:00:48,737 --> 00:00:57,975
Augmentation refers to enhancement of spontaneous contractions that are considered inadequate because of failed cervical dilation and poor fetal descent.

8
00:00:57,975 --> 00:01:04,862
This chapter presents indications and methods for labor induction or augmentation and for cervical ripening.

9
00:01:04,862 --> 00:01:06,837
Labor Induction.

10
00:01:06,837 --> 00:01:09,237
# Indications.

11
00:01:09,237 --> 00:01:18,975
In the United States, the incidence of labor induction rose from 9.5 percent in 1991 to 27 percent in 2019 .

12
00:01:18,975 --> 00:01:25,650
Induction is indicated when the benefits to either mother or fetus outweigh those of pregnancy continuation.

13
00:01:25,650 --> 00:01:41,912
The more common indications include membrane rupture without labor, gestational hypertension, oligohydramnios, nonreassuring fetal status, postterm pregnancy, and various maternal medical conditions such as chronic hypertension and diabetes .

14
00:01:41,912 --> 00:01:49,712
Methods to induce or augment labor are contraindicated by most conditions that preclude spontaneous labor or delivery.

15
00:01:49,712 --> 00:01:58,487
Maternal contraindications are an abnormally implanted placenta or a prior uterine incision type that is associated with a high rupture risk.

16
00:01:58,487 --> 00:02:06,500
Uncommon conditions are active genital herpes infection, contracted or distorted pelvic anatomy, or cervical cancer.

17
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:15,250
Fetal factors include appreciable macrosomia, severe hydrocephalus, malpresentation, or nonreassuring fetal status.

18
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:17,325
# Risks.

19
00:02:17,325 --> 00:02:26,725
Some maternal complications associated with labor induction are chorioamnionitis, uterine rupture, and postpartum hemorrhage from uterine atony.

20
00:02:26,725 --> 00:02:38,837
Earlier nonrandomized studies suggested a particularly higher risk for cesarean delivery in nulliparas undergoing labor induction (Luthy, 2004; Yeast, 1999).

21
00:02:38,837 --> 00:02:51,675
More recent ones, however, cite comparable or even lower rates of cesarean delivery when induced labor is compared with spontaneous labor (Middleton, 2020; Souter, 2019).

22
00:02:51,675 --> 00:03:00,212
These studies used spontaneous labor as the comparator, which may be less suitable than using expectant management as the comparator.

23
00:03:00,212 --> 00:03:17,575
In the ARRIVE trial—A Randomized Trial of Induction Versus Expectant Management-more than 6000 low-risk nulliparas at 39 weeks’ gestation were randomly assigned to labor induction or expectant management groups (Grobman, 2018; Tita, 2021).

24
00:03:17,575 --> 00:03:24,725
Primary outcome, which was the rate of severe neonatal morbidity or death, did not differ between cohorts.

25
00:03:24,725 --> 00:03:36,612
However, the cesarean delivery rate in the induction arm was significantly lower than that in the expectantly managed cohort—18.6 versus 22.2 percent, respectively.

26
00:03:36,612 --> 00:03:43,812
Rates of chorioamnionitis, postpartum hemorrhage, and peripartum infection were not significantly different.

27
00:03:43,812 --> 00:03:56,400
In a metaanalysis of six cohort studies, elective induction at 39 weeks’ gestation had a significantly lower risk of cesarean delivery and these other morbidities compared with expectant management .

28
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:58,950
Table 26-1.

29
00:03:58,950 --> 00:04:14,312
Selected Maternal and Perinatal Outcomes with Labor Induction Versus Expectant Management in Low-Risk Nulliparous Women— the ARRIVE Trial With induction, the overall associated risk of uterine rupture is low but is highest with a prior uterine scar .

30
00:04:14,312 --> 00:04:27,862
The American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (2019c) recommends against the use of prostaglandins for preinduction cervical ripening or for labor induction in women with a prior uterine incision.

31
00:04:27,862 --> 00:04:36,225
It recognizes labor induction with oxytocin as an option but also notes the higher potential rupture rate and lower VBAC rate.

32
00:04:36,225 --> 00:04:41,900
Oxytocin augmentation may be used in those undergoing TOLAC, although evidence

33
00:04:42,052 --> 00:04:45,052
for higher rupture rates are conflicting.

34
00:04:45,002 --> 00:04:50,227
Amniotomy is often selected to augment labor (p. 494).

35
00:04:50,227 --> 00:05:00,052
Of other potential risks, women whose labor is managed with amniotomy have a higher incidence of chorioamnionitis compared with those in spontaneous labor .

36
00:05:00,052 --> 00:05:13,002
In some, but not all studies, uterine atony and associated postpartum hemorrhage are more common in women undergoing induction or augmentation (Grobman, 2018; Widmer, 2020).

37
00:05:13,002 --> 00:05:25,489
And as discussed in Chapter 42 (p. 733), atony with intractable hemorrhage, especially following cesarean delivery, is a frequent indication for peripartum hysterectomy.

38
00:05:25,489 --> 00:05:35,489
In a study from Parkland Hospital, labor induction was associated with 17 percent of 553 unanticipated peripartum hysterectomies .

39
00:05:35,489 --> 00:05:38,439
# Elective Labor Induction.

40
00:05:38,439 --> 00:05:48,989
Until recently, the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (2019a) did not recommend elective labor induction at term for convenience.

41
00:05:48,989 --> 00:05:59,189
Occasional exceptions are risk of rapid labor, psychosocial indications, or logistics that factor family support availability and distance from the hospital.

42
00:05:59,189 --> 00:06:15,777
Importantly, several studies have shown that elective delivery before 39 completed weeks’ gestation is associated with significant adverse neonatal morbidity (Chiossi, 2013; Salemi, 2016; Tita, 2009).

43
00:06:15,777 --> 00:06:23,527
This proscription against elective induction at term was reconsidered following publication of the previously cited ARRIVE trial.

44
00:06:23,527 --> 00:06:41,952
Because of the results from that trial, the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (2018) and the Society for Maternal-Fetal Medicine (2019) conclude that offering elective induction to low-risk, well-dated nulliparas at 39 weeks’ gestation is reasonable.

45
00:06:41,952 --> 00:06:51,227
These women must meet the criteria for the ARRIVE trial, and it is recommended to combine shared decision-making with consideration of available resources.

46
00:06:51,227 --> 00:06:54,864
# Factors Affecting Induction Success.

47
00:06:54,864 --> 00:07:00,339
Several factors affect the ability of labor induction to achieve vaginal delivery.

48
00:07:00,339 --> 00:07:15,939
Favorable factors include younger age, multiparity, body mass index (BMI) <30, favorable cervix, and birthweight <3500 g (Freret, 2021; Sievert, 2017).

49
00:07:15,939 --> 00:07:20,752
In many cases, the uterus is simply poorly prepared for labor.

50
00:07:20,752 --> 00:07:24,827
One example is an “unripe” or “unfavorable” cervix.

51
00:07:24,827 --> 00:07:36,764
Indeed, investigators with the Consortium on Safe Labor reported that elective induction resulted in vaginal delivery in 97 percent of multiparas and 76 percent of nulliparas.

52
00:07:36,764 --> 00:07:40,714
Induction was more often successful with a “ripe cervix” .

53
00:07:40,714 --> 00:07:48,289
Failure of induction is likely strongly influenced by the induction duration, especially with an unfavorable cervix .

54
00:07:48,289 --> 00:07:56,489
In one study, labor duration to reach the active phase and to complete dilation was adversely affected by a higher BMI .

55
00:07:56,489 --> 00:08:00,502
Similar findings were reported for women with diabetes .

56
00:08:00,502 --> 00:08:15,014
Simon and Grobman (2005) concluded that a latent phase as long as 18 hours allowed most women undergoing labor induction to achieve a vaginal delivery without a significantly increased risk of maternal or neonatal morbidity.

57
00:08:15,014 --> 00:08:30,064
Rouse and associates (2000) recommend a minimum of 12 hours of uterine stimulation with oxytocin after membrane rupture, whereas Kawakita and coworkers (2016) recommend up to 15 hours for multiparas.

58
00:08:30,064 --> 00:08:32,714
Preinduction Cervical Ripening.

59
00:08:32,714 --> 00:08:39,727
As noted, a soft cervix—described as “ripe” or “favorable”—is important to successful labor induction.

60
00:08:39,727 --> 00:08:44,352
However, some estimates of favorability are highly subjective .

61
00:08:44,352 --> 00:08:52,389
Still, pharmacological and mechanical methods can enhance cervical qualities in a process of preinduction cervical ripening.

62
00:08:52,389 --> 00:08:57,602
Some of the techniques may have benefits compared with oxytocin induction alone .

63
00:08:57,602 --> 00:09:03,214
Namely, some are able to initiate labor and may effect delivery when used alone.

64
00:09:03,214 --> 00:09:14,702
However, few data support the premise that any of these methods lower cesarean delivery rates or lessen maternal or neonatal morbidity compared with women in whom these methods are not used.

65
00:09:14,702 --> 00:09:17,239
Table 26-2.

66
00:09:17,239 --> 00:09:26,852
Some Commonly Used Regimens Compared with Oxytocin Infusion for Preinduction Cervical Ripening and/or Labor Induction # Cervical “Favorability”.

67
00:09:26,852 --> 00:09:30,652
One quantifiable method to predict labor induction

68
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:38,070
outcomes is the score described by Bishop (1964) and presented in Table 26-3.

69
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:45,370
As favorability or Bishop score rises, the rate of induction to effect vaginal delivery also increases.

70
00:09:45,370 --> 00:09:53,945
A Bishop score >8 conveys a high likelihood for a successful induction, and a score ≤6 is considered unfavorable .

71
00:09:53,945 --> 00:09:56,445
Table 26-3.

72
00:09:56,445 --> 00:10:12,457
Bishop Scoring System Used for Assessment of Inducibility Laughon and coworkers (2011) attempted to simplify the Bishop score by performing a regression analysis on 5610 nulliparas with term singletons at 38 to 42 weeks’ gestation.

73
00:10:12,457 --> 00:10:19,532
Cervical dilation, station, and effacement were significantly associated with successful vaginal delivery.

74
00:10:19,532 --> 00:10:28,220
Thus, a simplified Bishop score had a similar or improved positive- or negative-predictive value compared with that of the original Bishop score.

75
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:37,495
Others have reported similar findings when consistency and position are omitted (Ivars, 2016; Raghuraman, 2016).

76
00:10:37,495 --> 00:10:44,432
Transvaginal sonographic measurement of cervical length has been evaluated as a Bishop score alternative .

77
00:10:44,432 --> 00:10:55,395
However, data from a metaanalysis of 31 trials showed overall low sensitivity and specificity and limited predictive utility to forecast successful induction .

78
00:10:55,395 --> 00:10:58,432
# Pharmacological Agents.

79
00:10:58,432 --> 00:11:02,357
Prostaglandin analogues make up available options.

80
00:11:02,357 --> 00:11:08,882
These can also stimulate contractions and thereby aid subsequent labor induction or augmentation.

81
00:11:08,882 --> 00:11:18,807
Importantly, in most studies of preinduction cervical ripening, oxytocin infusion either is initiated with the ripening agent or follows cervical change.

82
00:11:18,807 --> 00:11:21,732
# Prostaglandin E2.

83
00:11:21,732 --> 00:11:27,482
Dinoprostone is a synthetic analogue of prostaglandin E2 (PGE2).

84
00:11:27,482 --> 00:11:35,570
It is commercially available in three forms: a gel, a time-release vaginal insert, and a 20-mg suppository .

85
00:11:35,570 --> 00:11:43,020
The gel and time-release vaginal insert formulations are indicated only for cervical ripening before labor induction.

86
00:11:43,020 --> 00:11:49,070
Importantly, the 20-mg suppository is not indicated for cervical ripening.

87
00:11:49,070 --> 00:11:58,995
It instead is used for pregnancy termination between 12 and 20 weeks’ gestation and for evacuation of the uterus after fetal demise up to 28 weeks.

88
00:11:58,995 --> 00:12:11,482
Local application of the PGE2 gel form—Prepidil—is available in a 2.5mL syringe for an intracervical application of 0.5 mg of dinoprostone.

89
00:12:11,482 --> 00:12:20,807
With the woman supine, the tip of a prefilled syringe is placed intracervically, and the gel is deposited just below the internal cervical os.

90
00:12:20,807 --> 00:12:25,507
After application, the woman remains reclined for 30 minutes.

91
00:12:25,507 --> 00:12:32,707
Doses may be repeated every 6 hours, with a maximum of three doses recommended in 24 hours.

92
00:12:32,707 --> 00:12:39,445
A 10-mg dinoprostone vaginal insert—Cervidil—also is approved for cervical ripening.

93
00:12:39,445 --> 00:12:46,832
This is a thin, flat, rectangular polymeric wafer held within a small, white, mesh polyester sac .

94
00:12:46,832 --> 00:12:51,795
The sac has a long attached tail to allow easy removal from the vagina.

95
00:12:51,795 --> 00:12:58,845
The insert provides slower release of medication—0.3 mg/hr—than the gel form.

96
00:12:58,845 --> 00:13:04,770
Cervidil is used as a single dose placed transversely in the posterior vaginal fornix.

97
00:13:04,770 --> 00:13:11,570
Lubricant is used sparingly, if at all, because it can coat the device and hinder dinoprostone release.

98
00:13:11,570 --> 00:13:16,545
Following insertion, the woman remains recumbent for at least 2 hours.

99
00:13:16,545 --> 00:13:24,532
The insert is removed after 12 hours or with labor onset and at least 30 minutes before the administration of oxytocin.

100
00:13:24,532 --> 00:13:33,995
Since the active drug is encased in a mesh sac, one benefit is the ability for removal if fetal heart rate abnormalities or tachysystole develop.

101
00:13:33,995 --> 00:13:36,582
Figure 26-1.

102
00:13:36,582 --> 00:13:46,695
Cervidil vaginal insert contains 10 mg of dinoprostone designed to release approximately 0.3 mg/hr during a 10-hour period.

103
00:13:46,695 --> 00:13:53,670
Most metaanalyses of dinoprostone efficacy report a reduced time to delivery within 24 hours.

104
00:13:53,670 --> 00:13:59,132
However, they do not consistently show a reduction in the cesarean delivery rate.

105
00:13:59,132 --> 00:14:12,470
Thomas and colleagues (2014) provided a Cochrane review of 70 trials that included 11,487 women given vaginal prostaglandins or either placebo compared with no treatment.

106
00:14:12,470 --> 00:14:18,682
They noted a higher vaginal delivery rate within 24 hours when prostaglandins were used.

107
00:14:18,682 --> 00:14:28,670
They also reported a threefold greater risk of tachysystole accompanied by fetal heart rate changes, but cesarean delivery rates were not significantly decreased.

108
00:14:28,828 --> 00:14:34,753
Similar results were noted in another Cochrane review of intracervical dinoprostone gel .

109
00:14:34,703 --> 00:14:45,040
Compared with placebo or no treatment, a reduced risk of cesarean delivery was found only in a subgroup of women with an unfavorable cervix and intact membranes.

110
00:14:45,040 --> 00:15:02,128
Last, the Foley catheter versus vaginal PGE2 gel for induction of labor at term—PROBAAT-P and M trials—were unblinded, randomized trials comparing these two options (Jozwiak, 2011, 2013, 2014).

111
00:15:02,128 --> 00:15:08,603
The cesarean delivery rate did not differ, a finding consistent with accompanying metaanalyses.

112
00:15:08,603 --> 00:15:15,678
Side Effects Uterine tachysystole follows vaginally administered PGE2 in 1 to 5 percent of women .

113
00:15:15,678 --> 00:15:27,515
Although definitions of abnormal uterine activity vary among studies, most use the definition recommended by the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (2019b).

114
00:15:27,515 --> 00:15:32,728
Uterine tachysystole is defined as >5 contractions in a 10-minute period.

115
00:15:32,728 --> 00:15:38,640
It should always be qualified by the presence or absence of fetal heart rate abnormalities.

116
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:47,753
The terms uterine hypertonus, hyperstimulation, and hypercontractility are terms no longer defined, and their use is not recommended.

117
00:15:47,753 --> 00:15:58,528
Because uterine tachysystole associated with fetal compromise may develop when prostaglandins are used with preexisting spontaneous labor, such use is not recommended.

118
00:15:58,528 --> 00:16:07,503
If tachysystole follows the 10-mg insert, its removal by pulling on the tail of the surrounding net sac will usually reverse this effect.

119
00:16:07,503 --> 00:16:12,365
Irrigation to remove the gel preparation has not been shown to be helpful.

120
00:16:12,365 --> 00:16:18,765
The manufacturers recommend caution when these preparations are used in women with ruptured membranes.

121
00:16:18,765 --> 00:16:23,415
This concern is also extended to women with glaucoma or asthma.

122
00:16:23,415 --> 00:16:32,340
However, in a review of 189 women with asthma, dinoprostone was not associated with asthma worsening or exacerbation .

123
00:16:32,340 --> 00:16:50,028
Other contraindications listed by the manufacturers include prior dinoprostone hypersensitivity, suspicion of fetal compromise or cephalopelvic disproportion, unexplained vaginal bleeding, six or more prior term pregnancies, and contraindications to vaginal delivery.

124
00:16:50,028 --> 00:17:04,065
Others are women already receiving oxytocin, those with a contraindication to oxytocin, or those who may be endangered by prolonged uterine contractions, for example, those with prior cesarean delivery or uterine surgery.

125
00:17:04,065 --> 00:17:10,678
Administration PGE2 preparations should be administered only in or near the delivery suite.

126
00:17:10,678 --> 00:17:15,465
Moreover, uterine activity and fetal heart rate should be monitored .

127
00:17:15,465 --> 00:17:19,690
These guidelines stem from the risk of uterine tachysystole.

128
00:17:19,690 --> 00:17:27,140
When contractions begin, they are usually apparent in the first hour and show peak activity in the first 4 hours.

129
00:17:27,140 --> 00:17:42,853
According to manufacturer guidelines, oxytocin induction that follows prostaglandin use for cervical ripening should be delayed for 6 to 12 hours following PGE2 gel administration or for at least 30 minutes after removal of the vaginal insert.

130
00:17:42,853 --> 00:17:45,703
# Prostaglandin E1.

131
00:17:45,703 --> 00:17:56,665
Misoprostol—Cytotec—is a synthetic prostaglandin E1 (PGE1) that is approved as a 100- or 200-µg tablet for peptic ulcer prevention.

132
00:17:56,665 --> 00:18:01,940
These tablets can be split to administer 25- or 50-µg doses.

133
00:18:01,940 --> 00:18:06,903
The drug is absorbed from both vaginal, oral, and buccal administration.

134
00:18:06,903 --> 00:18:15,228
Randomized trials of labor induction with misoprostol have evaluated various induction regimens with differing primary outcomes .

135
00:18:15,228 --> 00:18:17,803
Table 26-4.

136
00:18:17,803 --> 00:18:31,128
Randomized Trials with 200 or More Subjects Designed to Compare Misoprostol (PGE1) With or Without Foley Bulb Misoprostol is widely used “off label” safely for preinduction cervical ripening .

137
00:18:31,128 --> 00:18:39,503
The tablets are stable at room temperature, and the drug currently is the preferred prostaglandin for cervical ripening at Parkland Hospital.

138
00:18:39,503 --> 00:18:52,765
Vaginal Administration Compared with intracervical or intravaginal PGE2, vaginally administered misoprostol tablets offer equivalent or superior efficacy for cervical ripening or labor induction .

139
00:18:52,765 --> 00:19:03,265
Compared with oxytocin or with intravaginal or intracervical dinoprostone, vaginal misoprostol increased the vaginal delivery rate within 24 hours.

140
00:19:03,265 --> 00:19:09,440
Although the uterine tachysystole rate was higher, this did not affect cesarean delivery rates.

141
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:11,765
Moreover, compared

142
00:19:11,932 --> 00:19:20,969
with dinoprostone, misoprostol lowered the need for oxytocin induction, but it raised the frequency of meconium-stained amnionic fluid.

143
00:19:20,919 --> 00:19:31,382
Higher doses of misoprostol are associated with a decreased need for oxytocin but with greater rates of uterine tachysystole, with and without fetal heart rate changes.

144
00:19:31,382 --> 00:19:39,744
The American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (2019a) recommends a 25-µg vaginal dose.

145
00:19:39,744 --> 00:19:44,532
The drug is evenly distributed among 100-µg tablets that are quartered.

146
00:19:44,532 --> 00:19:54,494
Oral Administration PGE1 tablets are also effective when given orally, but with a faster peak concentration and decline compared with the vaginal route.

147
00:19:54,494 --> 00:20:09,932
One Cochrane metaanalysis of 76 trials reported that oral misoprostol compared with placebo significantly increased the rate of vaginal birth within 24 hours, while decreasing the need for oxytocin and lowering the cesarean delivery rate .

148
00:20:09,932 --> 00:20:20,819
Comparisons of oral misoprostol and oxytocin and of oral misoprostol and dinoprostone also found significantly reduced rates of cesarean delivery with misoprostol.

149
00:20:20,819 --> 00:20:32,894
Similar efficacy was noted between oral misoprostol and vaginal administration, although oral administration was associated with significantly higher Apgar scores and less postpartum hemorrhage.

150
00:20:32,894 --> 00:20:43,057
Thorbiörnson and associates (2017) also reported lower rates of cesarean delivery with oral misoprostol compared with vaginal dinoprostone.

151
00:20:43,057 --> 00:20:46,032
# Nitric Oxide Donors.

152
00:20:46,032 --> 00:20:52,682
Over the years, agents that stimulate nitric oxide production have been studied for labor induction.

153
00:20:52,682 --> 00:20:58,007
Physiologically, nitric oxide is likely a mediator of cervical ripening.

154
00:20:58,007 --> 00:21:04,769
Cervical nitric oxide metabolite concentrations are increased at the beginning of uterine contractions.

155
00:21:04,769 --> 00:21:13,544
Both isosorbide mononitrate and glyceryl trinitrate have been studied but are less effective clinically than prostaglandins for cervical ripening.

156
00:21:13,544 --> 00:21:29,144
In one metaanalysis, the rate of cesarean delivery was not reduced in those given nitric oxide donors compared with those given placebo, intravaginal or intracervical prostaglandins, intravaginal misoprostol, or intracervical catheter .

157
00:21:29,144 --> 00:21:36,357
However, nitric oxide donors were associated with significantly more headaches, nausea, and vomiting.

158
00:21:36,357 --> 00:21:39,132
# Mechanical Techniques.

159
00:21:39,132 --> 00:21:49,757
These include transcervical placement of a Foley catheter, with or without extraamnionic saline infusion; hygroscopic cervical dilators; and membrane stripping.

160
00:21:49,757 --> 00:22:00,057
In one metaanalysis, mechanical methods reduced the risk of uterine tachysystole compared with prostaglandins, although cesarean delivery rates were unchanged .

161
00:22:00,057 --> 00:22:07,544
Trials comparing mechanical techniques and oxytocin found a lower rate of cesarean delivery with mechanical methods.

162
00:22:07,544 --> 00:22:16,369
Trials comparing mechanical options with dinoprostone found a higher rate of multiparas undelivered at 24 hours with mechanical methods.

163
00:22:16,369 --> 00:22:28,407
In another metaanalysis comparing Foley catheter and intravaginal dinoprostone inserts, cesarean delivery rates were similar, but uterine tachysystole was less frequent with catheter use .

164
00:22:28,407 --> 00:22:37,432
Transcervical Catheter Generally, this option is only used with an unfavorable cervix because the catheter comes out as the cervix opens.

165
00:22:37,432 --> 00:22:41,857
It is suitable for women with membranes that are intact or ruptured.

166
00:22:41,857 --> 00:22:51,119
In most cases, a Foley catheter is placed through the internal cervical os, and downward tension is created by taping the catheter to the thigh .

167
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:56,094
Extraamnionic saline infusion (EASI) is one modification.

168
00:22:56,094 --> 00:23:03,444
It adds a constant saline infusion through the catheter into the space between the internal os and placental membranes .

169
00:23:03,444 --> 00:23:13,044
In one study, chorioamnionitis was significantly less frequent when infusion was added compared with no infusion—6 versus 16 percent .

170
00:23:13,044 --> 00:23:21,232
Similarly, in a metaanalysis, transcervical catheters were not associated with higher rates of maternal or fetal infection .

171
00:23:21,232 --> 00:23:23,769
Figure 26-2.

172
00:23:23,769 --> 00:23:31,107
Extraamnionic saline infusion (EASI) through a 26F Foley catheter that is placed through the cervix.

173
00:23:31,107 --> 00:23:39,432
The 30-mL balloon is inflated with saline and pulled snugly against the internal os, and the catheter is taped to the thigh.

174
00:23:39,432 --> 00:23:47,407
Room-temperature normal saline is infused through the catheter port of the Foley at 30 or 40 mL/hour by intravenous

175
00:23:47,572 --> 00:23:49,534
infusion pump.

176
00:23:49,484 --> 00:23:57,259
As discussed earlier, transcervical catheters do not reduce the cesarean delivery rate compared with prostaglandins.

177
00:23:57,259 --> 00:24:20,184
There were several iterations of the PROBAAT trials—I, P, M, and II—in which cervical ripening with a Foley catheter was compared with vaginal dinoprostone gel, dinoprostone vaginal inserts, and vaginal or oral misoprostol (Jozwiak, 2011, 2013, 2014; Ten Eikelder, 2016).

178
00:24:20,184 --> 00:24:26,509
These studies reported similar outcomes between the mechanical methods and the prostaglandin agents.

179
00:24:26,509 --> 00:24:33,272
Also, fewer overall cases of cardiotocographic changes were seen in the mechanical technique group.

180
00:24:33,272 --> 00:24:38,209
Similar cesarean delivery rates are found in other comparison studies.

181
00:24:38,209 --> 00:24:50,672
Schoen and coworkers (2017) observed that concurrent oxytocin with a transcervical Foley catheter shortened the median time to delivery compared with a Foley catheter followed by oxytocin.

182
00:24:50,672 --> 00:24:54,909
However, rates of cesarean delivery were unchanged.

183
00:24:54,909 --> 00:25:03,684
Connolly and associates (2016) reported similar findings for women within intact membranes undergoing labor induction.

184
00:25:03,684 --> 00:25:15,084
Amorosa and colleagues (2017) found no benefit for transcervical catheter coupled with oxytocin compared with oxytocin alone for women with ruptured membranes.

185
00:25:15,084 --> 00:25:26,447
Other studies of concurrent misoprostol reported reduced time to delivery without affecting cesarean delivery rates (Carbone, 2013; Levine, 2016).

186
00:25:26,447 --> 00:25:35,322
With catheter induction plus misoprostol, one randomized trial found vaginal misoprostol to be superior to buccal administration .

187
00:25:35,322 --> 00:25:40,372
Last, addition of tension does not appear to enhance catheter efficacy .

188
00:25:40,372 --> 00:25:51,422
These investigators randomly assigned 140 women to transcervical Foley catheter placement, with and without tension, and reported similar vaginal delivery rates.

189
00:25:51,422 --> 00:25:58,159
One large trial at Parkland Hospital evaluated the addition of a Foley catheter to oral misoprostol.

190
00:25:58,159 --> 00:26:07,172
With catheter addition, investigators found no improvement in the vaginal delivery rate, but the chorioamnionitis rate was 30-percent higher .

191
00:26:07,172 --> 00:26:13,897
The unaltered vaginal delivery rate persisted in a stratified analysis of nulliparas and multiparas.

192
00:26:13,897 --> 00:26:22,184
In this study, our standard labor induction protocol with misoprostol alone achieved a 77percent vaginal delivery rate.

193
00:26:22,184 --> 00:26:33,834
Hygroscopic Cervical Dilators Cervical dilation can be accomplished using hygroscopic or osmotic cervical dilators, which are illustrated in Chapter 11 (p. 209).

194
00:26:33,834 --> 00:26:40,034
Briefly, these include Laminaria japonicum or hygroscopic devices (Dilapan-S).

195
00:26:40,034 --> 00:26:46,447
Intuitive concerns of ascending infection have not been verified, and their use appears to be safe.

196
00:26:46,447 --> 00:26:52,422
Placement generally requires a speculum and positioning of the woman on an examination table.

197
00:26:52,422 --> 00:26:58,722
Studies comparing hygroscopic cervical dilators and prostaglandins found few benefits .

198
00:26:58,722 --> 00:27:01,822
Methods Of Induction And Augmentation.

199
00:27:01,822 --> 00:27:06,722
Oxytocin has been used for labor induction for more than 70 years .

200
00:27:06,722 --> 00:27:14,234
As discussed, other methods now include prostaglandins, which are used alone or in combination with oxytocin.

201
00:27:14,234 --> 00:27:18,559
Prostaglandins include misoprostol and dinoprostone.

202
00:27:18,559 --> 00:27:30,159
Mechanical methods encompass membrane stripping, artificial rupture of membranes, extraamnionic saline infusion, transcervical balloons, and hygroscopic cervical dilators.

203
00:27:30,159 --> 00:27:41,059
As recommended in Guidelines for Perinatal Care, each obstetrical department should have written protocols that describe administration of these methods for labor induction and augmentation .

204
00:27:41,059 --> 00:27:51,034
Because preinduction cervical ripening frequently prompts labor, studies to determine induction efficacy for some of these agents have produced confusing results.

205
00:27:51,034 --> 00:27:59,272
The use of prostaglandins for labor augmentation has generally been considered experimental due to high rates of uterine tachysystole.

206
00:27:59,272 --> 00:28:02,122
# Prostaglandin E1.

207
00:28:02,122 --> 00:28:08,247
Both vaginal and oral misoprostol are used for either cervical ripening or labor induction.

208
00:28:08,247 --> 00:28:22,934
For labor induction in women at or near term with either prematurely ruptured membranes or a favorable cervix, 100 µg of oral or 25 µg of vaginal misoprostol has similar efficacy compared with intravenous oxytocin.

209
00:28:22,934 --> 00:28:34,147
From these studies, evidence supports that oral misoprostol may be superior (Alfirevic, 2014; Hofmeyr, 2010; Lo, 2003).

210
00:28:34,147 --> 00:28:35,784
That said,

211
00:28:35,956 --> 00:28:42,893
misoprostol is associated with a greater rate of uterine tachysystole, particularly at higher doses.

212
00:28:42,843 --> 00:28:51,006
Also, induction with PGE1 may prove ineffective and require subsequent induction or augmentation with oxytocin.

213
00:28:51,006 --> 00:28:59,831
Thus, although there are trade-offs regarding the risks, costs, and ease of administration of each drug, either is suitable for labor induction.

214
00:28:59,831 --> 00:29:08,756
At Parkland Hospital, we administer an initial oral 100-µg dose, which may be repeated for inadequate labor after 6 hours.

215
00:29:08,756 --> 00:29:17,643
Four hours after the second dose or in those with tachysystole, an oxytocin infusion is begun, if needed, for hypotonic labor.

216
00:29:17,643 --> 00:29:25,593
One study compared oral misoprostol and a newer misoprostol vaginal insert that releases drug up to 24 hours.

217
00:29:25,593 --> 00:29:35,168
With the insert, cesarean delivery and adverse neonatal outcome rates were higher, but time to delivery was shorter (Döbert, 2018).

218
00:29:35,168 --> 00:29:45,156
Additional studies found these adverse outcomes were mitigated if the insert time was limited to 10 hours (Brandstetter, 2019, 2020).

219
00:29:45,156 --> 00:29:57,618
For labor augmentation, results of a randomized controlled trial showed oral misoprostol, 75 µg given at 4-hour intervals for a maximum of two doses, to be safe and effective .

220
00:29:57,618 --> 00:30:10,956
Although the uterine tachysystole rate was higher among women with labor augmented with misoprostol, the frequency of nonreassuring fetal status or cesarean delivery did not differ between oxytocin and misoprostol.

221
00:30:10,956 --> 00:30:13,306
# Oxytocin.

222
00:30:13,306 --> 00:30:21,593
As previously emphasized, in many instances, preinduction cervical ripening and labor induction are simply a continuum.

223
00:30:21,593 --> 00:30:25,356
In this regard “ripening” can also stimulate labor.

224
00:30:25,356 --> 00:30:32,731
If not, induction or augmentation may be continued with solutions of oxytocin given by infusion pump.

225
00:30:32,731 --> 00:30:41,106
Its use in augmentation is a key component in the active management of labor, described in Chapter 22 (p. 430).

226
00:30:41,106 --> 00:30:51,743
With oxytocin use, the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (2019a) recommends fetal heart rate and uterine contraction monitoring.

227
00:30:51,743 --> 00:30:56,881
Contractions can be monitored either by palpation or by electronic means.

228
00:30:56,881 --> 00:31:03,406
Intravenous Oxytocin Administration A 1-mL vial contains 10 units of oxytocin.

229
00:31:03,406 --> 00:31:14,843
A typical infusate consists of 10 or 20 units, which is 10,000 or 20,000 mU, respectively, mixed into 1000 mL of crystalloid or dextrose solution.

230
00:31:14,843 --> 00:31:24,006
This mixture results in an oxytocin concentration of 10 or 20 mU/mL, respectively, and is administered by infusion pump.

231
00:31:24,006 --> 00:31:31,731
To avoid bolus administration, the infusion should be inserted into the main intravenous line close to the venipuncture site.

232
00:31:31,731 --> 00:31:42,856
The goal of induction or augmentation is to effect uterine activity sufficient to produce cervical change and fetal descent, while avoiding development of a nonreassuring fetal status.

233
00:31:42,856 --> 00:31:52,431
According to the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (2019a), the latter is a category III fetal heart rate tracing.

234
00:31:52,431 --> 00:32:06,393
In general, oxytocin is discontinued if the number of contractions persists with a frequency of more than five in a 10-minute period or more than seven in a 15-minute period or with a persistent nonreassuring fetal heart rate pattern.

235
00:32:06,393 --> 00:32:12,093
Oxytocin discontinuation nearly always rapidly lowers contraction frequency.

236
00:32:12,093 --> 00:32:20,431
When oxytocin is stopped, its concentration in plasma rapidly falls because the half-life is approximately 3 to 5 minutes.

237
00:32:20,431 --> 00:32:29,268
The uterus contracts within 3 to 5 minutes of beginning an oxytocin infusion, and a plasma steady state is reached in 40 minutes .

238
00:32:29,268 --> 00:32:39,206
Response varies greatly and depends on preexisting uterine activity, cervical status, pregnancy duration, and individual biological differences.

239
00:32:39,206 --> 00:32:50,106
CaldeyroBarcia and Poseiro (1960) reported that the uterine response to oxytocin increases from 20 to 30 weeks’ gestation and rises rapidly at term.

240
00:32:50,106 --> 00:32:54,956
Oxytocin is generally very successful when used to stimulate labor.

241
00:32:54,956 --> 00:33:07,781
In one large Cochrane metaanalysis, oxytocin was compared with expectant management, and fewer women—8 versus 54 percent—failed to deliver vaginally within 24 hours with oxytocin .

242
00:33:07,781 --> 00:33:12,156
This analysis studied different oxytocin dosing regimens.

243
00:33:12,156 --> 00:33:19,993
Oxytocin Regimens Several evidence-based regimens for labor stimulation are now recommended by the American College of

244
00:33:20,164 --> 00:33:24,401
Obstetricians and Gynecologists (2019a).

245
00:33:24,351 --> 00:33:28,339
These and others are shown in Table 26-5.

246
00:33:28,339 --> 00:33:34,089
Initially, only variations of low-dose protocols were used in the United States.

247
00:33:34,089 --> 00:33:48,676
Subsequently, O’Driscoll and colleagues (1984) described their Dublin protocol for the active management of labor that called for oxytocin at a starting dosage of 6 mU/min and advanced in 6-mU/min increments.

248
00:33:48,676 --> 00:34:04,076
Subsequent comparative trials during the 1990s studied high-dose (4 to 6 mU/min) versus conventional low-dose (0.5 to 1.5 mU/min) regimens, both for labor induction and for augmentation.

249
00:34:04,076 --> 00:34:06,689
Table 26-5.

250
00:34:06,689 --> 00:34:24,026
Various Low- and High-Dose Oxytocin Regimens Used for Labor Induction From Parkland Hospital, Satin and associates (1992) evaluated an oxytocin regimen using an initial and incremental dosage of 6 mU/min compared with one using 1 mU/min.

251
00:34:24,026 --> 00:34:36,589
Among 1112 women undergoing induction, the 6-mU/min regimen resulted in a shorter mean admission-todelivery time, fewer failed inductions, and no cases of neonatal sepsis.

252
00:34:36,589 --> 00:34:54,951
Among 1676 women who had labor augmentation, those who received the 6mU/min regimen had a shorter duration-to-delivery time, fewer forceps deliveries, fewer cesarean deliveries for dystocia, and lower rates of intrapartum chorioamnionitis or neonatal sepsis.

253
00:34:54,951 --> 00:35:04,789
With this protocol, uterine tachysystole was managed by oxytocin discontinuation followed by resumption when indicated and at half the stopping dosage.

254
00:35:04,789 --> 00:35:15,139
Thereafter, the dosage was increased at 3 mU/min when appropriate, instead of the usual 6mU/min increase used for women without tachysystole.

255
00:35:15,139 --> 00:35:18,564
No adverse neonatal effects were observed.

256
00:35:18,564 --> 00:35:26,176
More recently, Son and colleagues (2021) confirmed these findings in a randomized clinical trial.

257
00:35:26,176 --> 00:35:36,414
In 1990 at Parkland Hospital, routine use of the 6-mU/min oxytocin beginning and incremental dosage was incorporated and continues through today.

258
00:35:36,414 --> 00:35:44,064
In other labor units, a 2-mU/min beginning and incremental oxytocin regimen is preferred and administered.

259
00:35:44,064 --> 00:35:49,751
With either regimen, dosages are employed for either labor induction or augmentation.

260
00:35:49,751 --> 00:35:56,801
Interval Between Incremental Dosing Intervals to increase oxytocin doses vary from 15 to 40 minutes .

261
00:35:56,801 --> 00:36:07,351
Satin and associates (1994) addressed this aspect with a 6-mU/min regimen providing increases at either 20- or 40-minute intervals.

262
00:36:07,351 --> 00:36:20,114
Women assigned to the 20-minute interval regimen for labor augmentation had a significantly reduced cesarean delivery rate for dystocia compared with that for the 40-minute interval regimen—8 versus 12 percent.

263
00:36:20,114 --> 00:36:27,639
As perhaps expected, uterine tachysystole was significantly more frequent with the 20minute escalation regimen.

264
00:36:27,639 --> 00:36:32,664
Other investigators reported even more frequent incremental increases.

265
00:36:32,664 --> 00:36:44,001
Frigoletto (1995) and Xenakis (1995) and their coworkers gave oxytocin at 4 mU/min with increases as needed every 15 minutes.

266
00:36:44,001 --> 00:36:52,451
Merrill and Zlatnik (1999) started with 4.5-mU/min doses and increased this every 30 minutes.

267
00:36:52,451 --> 00:37:00,089
López-Zeno and associates (1992) used 6-mU/min doses and 15-minute intervals.

268
00:37:00,089 --> 00:37:08,389
Maximal Oxytocin Dosage The maximal effective dose of oxytocin to achieve adequate contractions in all women is different.

269
00:37:08,389 --> 00:37:19,826
In one study of 1151 consecutive nulliparas, the likelihood of progression to vaginal delivery decreased at and beyond an oxytocin dosage of 36 mU/min .

270
00:37:19,826 --> 00:37:26,314
Still, at a dosage of 72 mU/min, half of the nulliparas were delivered vaginally.

271
00:37:26,314 --> 00:37:41,164
Thus, if contractions are not adequate—less than 200 Montevideo units—and if the fetal status is reassuring and labor has arrested, an oxytocin infusion dose greater than 48 mU/min has no apparent risks .

272
00:37:41,164 --> 00:37:44,126
# Risks versus Benefits.

273
00:37:44,126 --> 00:37:51,814
Unless the uterus is scarred, uterine rupture associated with oxytocin infusion is rare, even in parous women.

274
00:37:51,814 --> 00:38:02,926
Flannelly and associates (1993) reported no cases of uterine rupture, with or without oxytocin, in 27,829 nulliparas.

275
00:38:02,926 --> 00:38:10,364
Eight instances of overt uterine rupture during labor were noted in 48,718 parous women.

276
00:38:10,364 --> 00:38:14,264
Only one of these was associated with oxytocin use.

277
00:38:14,264 --> 00:38:25,839
A population- based retrospective review from Denmark reported a rupture rate of 3.3 per 100,000 women without prior cesarean, with the highest risk among multiparas .

278
00:38:25,839 --> 00:38:27,776
Our experience

279
00:38:27,940 --> 00:38:34,652
from Parkland Hospital is that oxytocin induction and augmentation are associated with uterine rupture.

280
00:38:34,602 --> 00:38:46,465
During an 8-year period in which there were almost 95,000 births, 15 women suffered a primary uterine rupture, and 14 of these cases were associated with oxytocin use.

281
00:38:46,465 --> 00:38:52,715
In half of these women, prostaglandins were also given before augmentation with oxytocin.

282
00:38:52,715 --> 00:39:01,502
Oxytocin has amino-acid homology similar to arginine vasopressin (AVP) and has significant antidiuretic action.

283
00:39:01,502 --> 00:39:08,115
When infused at doses of 20 mU/min or more, renal free water clearance drops markedly.

284
00:39:08,115 --> 00:39:17,890
If aqueous fluids are infused in appreciable amounts along with oxytocin, water intoxication can lead to convulsions, coma, and even death.

285
00:39:17,890 --> 00:39:29,365
In general, if oxytocin is to be administered in high doses for a considerable period of time, its concentration should be increased rather than raising the flow rate of a more dilute solution.

286
00:39:29,365 --> 00:39:36,252
Consideration also should be given to use of crystalloids—either normal saline or lactated Ringer solution.

287
00:39:36,252 --> 00:39:39,440
# Uterine Contraction Pressures.

288
00:39:39,440 --> 00:39:46,677
Contraction forces in spontaneously laboring women range from 90 to 390 Montevideo units .

289
00:39:46,677 --> 00:40:03,090
Early researchers found that the mean or median spontaneous uterine contraction pattern between 140 and 150 Montevideo units resulted in progression to vaginal delivery (CaldeyroBarcia, 1950; Seitchik, 1984).

290
00:40:03,090 --> 00:40:09,540
Labor arrest in first-stage labor is described in Chapter 23 (p. 434).

291
00:40:09,540 --> 00:40:20,352
In the management of active-phase arrest, and with no contraindication to intravenous oxytocin, decisions must be made with knowledge of the safe upper range of uterine activity.

292
00:40:20,352 --> 00:40:29,027
Hauth and colleagues (1986) described an effective and safe protocol for oxytocin augmentation for active-phase arrest.

293
00:40:29,027 --> 00:40:36,777
With it, more than 90 percent of women achieved an average of at least 200 to 225 Montevideo units.

294
00:40:36,777 --> 00:40:45,790
They later reported that nearly all women in whom active-phase arrest persisted despite oxytocin generated more than 200 Montevideo units .

295
00:40:45,790 --> 00:40:54,902
Importantly, despite no labor progression, no adverse maternal or perinatal effects were noted in those ultimately requiring cesarean delivery.

296
00:40:54,902 --> 00:41:05,102
Data regarding the safety and efficacy of contraction patterns in women with a prior cesarean delivery, with twins, or with an overdistended uterus are lacking.

297
00:41:05,102 --> 00:41:09,052
# Amniotomy for Induction and Augmentation.

298
00:41:09,052 --> 00:41:14,352
Elective amniotomy with the intention of accelerating labor is often performed.

299
00:41:14,352 --> 00:41:23,752
For labor induction, artificial rupture of the membranes— sometimes called surgical induction—can be used and always implies a commitment to delivery.

300
00:41:23,752 --> 00:41:32,315
The main disadvantage of amniotomy used alone for labor induction is the unpredictable and occasionally long interval until labor onset.

301
00:41:32,315 --> 00:41:43,777
That said, in a randomized trial, Bakos and Bäckström (1987) found that amniotomy alone or combined with oxytocin was superior to oxytocin alone.

302
00:41:43,777 --> 00:41:57,140
Mercer and colleagues (1995) randomly assigned 209 women undergoing oxytocin induction to either early amniotomy at 1 to 2 cm or late amniotomy at 5 cm.

303
00:41:57,140 --> 00:42:02,402
Early amniotomy was associated with a 4-hour reduction in labor duration.

304
00:42:02,402 --> 00:42:08,277
With early amniotomy, however, the incidence of chorioamnionitis was elevated.

305
00:42:08,277 --> 00:42:20,090
In a metaanalysis, De Vivo and associates (2020) reported that early amniotomy did not increase the risk of cesarean delivery yet reduced the interval from induction to delivery.

306
00:42:20,090 --> 00:42:26,127
For labor augmentation, amniotomy is commonly performed when labor is abnormally slow.

307
00:42:26,127 --> 00:42:36,352
Shown in Table 26-6, amniotomy at approximately 5-cm dilation accelerated spontaneous labor by 1 to 1½ hours.

308
00:42:36,352 --> 00:42:43,540
Importantly, neither the need for oxytocin stimulation nor the overall cesarean delivery rate was higher.

309
00:42:43,540 --> 00:42:53,665
Although the incidences of mild and moderate cord compression patterns were increased following amniotomy, cesarean delivery rates for fetal distress were not greater.

310
00:42:53,665 --> 00:42:57,952
Most importantly, there were no adverse perinatal effects.

311
00:42:57,952 --> 00:43:00,577
Table 26-6.

312
00:43:00,577 --> 00:43:17,402
Randomized Clinical Trials of Elective Amniotomy in Early Spontaneous Labor at Term Rouse and associates (1994) also found that amniotomy with oxytocin augmentation for arrested active-phase labor shortened the time to delivery by 44 minutes

313
00:43:17,572 --> 00:43:20,572
compared with that of oxytocin alone.

314
00:43:20,522 --> 00:43:29,147
Although amniotomy did not alter the delivery route, one drawback was that it significantly increased the incidence of chorioamnionitis.

315
00:43:29,147 --> 00:43:35,072
Regardless of the indication, amniotomy is associated with a risk of cord prolapse.

316
00:43:35,072 --> 00:43:41,059
To minimize this risk, disengagement of the fetal head during amniotomy is avoided.

317
00:43:41,059 --> 00:43:46,047
Toward this goal, fundal or suprapubic pressure or both may be helpful.

318
00:43:46,047 --> 00:43:50,497
Some clinicians prefer to rupture membranes during a contraction.

319
00:43:50,497 --> 00:44:06,572
If the vertex is not well applied to the lower uterine segment, a gradual egress of amnionic fluid can sometimes be accomplished by several membrane punctures with a 26-gauge needle held with a ring forceps and with direct visualization using a vaginal speculum.

320
00:44:06,572 --> 00:44:14,472
Alternatively, the trumpet used for pudendal blockade can sheath the needle and manually guide it through the cervix for amniotomy.

321
00:44:14,472 --> 00:44:20,009
In many of these cases, however, membranes tear and fluid is lost rapidly.

322
00:44:20,009 --> 00:44:28,984
Because of the risk of cord prolapse, or rarely placental abruption, the fetal heart rate is assessed before and immediately after amniotomy.

323
00:44:28,984 --> 00:44:32,547
# Membrane Stripping for Labor Induction.

324
00:44:32,547 --> 00:44:37,397
Labor induction by membrane “stripping” or “sweeping” is a frequent practice.

325
00:44:37,397 --> 00:44:49,022
Several studies have suggested that membrane stripping is safe and lowers the incidence of postterm pregnancy without consistently raising the incidence of ruptured membranes, infection, or bleeding.

326
00:44:49,022 --> 00:44:55,447
Randomized trials are limited and a metaanalysis of two of these reported sweeping to be ineffective .

327
00:44:55,447 --> 00:44:59,072
Downsides are discomfort and associated bleeding .

